WEBVTT

00:00:00.025 --> 00:00:04.973
Northbridge Commercial Bank wants to know
where its analysts' time goes.

00:00:04.973 --> 00:00:09.440
It sends an extract of its alerts, rules,
dispositions and cases.

00:00:09.440 --> 00:00:12.052
The data in this film is illustrative.

00:00:12.765 --> 00:00:16.264
Northbridge is onboarded as an evaluation
engagement.

00:00:16.264 --> 00:00:21.811
Its due diligence is approved by a second
person, its data is processed under a data

00:00:21.811 --> 00:00:27.687
processing agreement, and the term and the
deletion date are set before any data arrives.

00:00:27.687 --> 00:00:31.649
Our external-manager film walks through each
of those steps.

00:00:33.249 --> 00:00:34.481
Four files load.

00:00:34.481 --> 00:00:39.255
One alert has no identifier, so it is
quarantined and counted:

00:00:39.255 --> 00:00:41.488
three accepted, one rejected.

00:00:42.199 --> 00:00:47.963
The extract is frozen in a fingerprinted
snapshot and run through the platform's alert

00:00:47.963 --> 00:00:51.449
intelligence and financial crime operations
engines.

00:00:52.149 --> 00:00:58.136
The findings show where alerts close without
action, rule by rule, with recommendations and

00:00:58.136 --> 00:00:58.794
a roadmap.

00:00:59.499 --> 00:01:02.923
The compliance officer downloads the findings
pack:

00:01:02.923 --> 00:01:06.213
the report, and the rule-level results behind
it.

00:01:09.999 --> 00:01:11.937
This time the bank subscribes.

00:01:11.937 --> 00:01:15.941
Commercial drafts the subscription, and
Revenue provisions it.

00:01:20.749 --> 00:01:23.261
The evaluation closes as converted.

00:01:23.261 --> 00:01:24.624
Nothing is deleted.

00:01:24.624 --> 00:01:29.504
The data stays with the customer, and the
evaluation banner is gone.

00:01:32.999 --> 00:01:38.995
The compliance officer reopens the assessment
from the evaluation, exactly as it was.

00:01:38.995 --> 00:01:43.086
From an extract to a customer, without
reloading anything.
